 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Open: shape-template sampling shortcut
+
+Bounded review of generator SHA-256
+`a4d59f7331fe3e8ed9ea0303b0fdc4d3944673bd15de15ea8b32bdbad2a44a81`
+found that a rival can replace every observed insert with the constructor's
+deterministic corner-notch template, using only its dimensions and color.
+Canonical and rival Racket programs agree on all eight tested emitted grids
+(seeds 0–7, sample index 0). Two of those grids form the retained demonstrations.
+Rotating one insert's pixels 180 degrees inside its unchanged bounding box
+produces a validator-accepted query that separates the programs. All 18 labels
+were executed through protected Racket.
+
+Evidence: `counterexamples/shape-template-shortcut.json`; executable probe:
+`workspace/review_tools/teaching_probe.py`. Reproduce from the packet root with
+`python3 review.py run python3 generators/39a07044b798/workspace/review_tools/teaching_probe.py --out ../checks/39a07044b798/new-witness.json`.
+
+The distinguishing query is outside the present shape constructor's support.
+This is a shape-diversity/teaching limitation, not an observed wrong label on a
+generated query or a prevalence estimate. The rule itself remains unchanged.
+Next useful repair: vary connected bbox-exact insert shapes and include a
+shape-sensitive demonstration while preserving dimension matching and rotation.
+The two executable interpretations and their predictions are retained for
+optional alternative-solution research, with no extra official gold label.
