 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Open: an emitted three-demo lesson can omit the orientation contrast
+
+On generator SHA-256
+`8db192822a20cbf1050ad2c4524ff60a3a615e2ab2904114bb6a8f051f2782c6`,
+the first bounded consecutive-window witness uses seeds 11, 12, 13 as demos
+and seed 14 as query (all sample index 0). The demos lack a vertical red triple,
+so a rival that recolors the center of either horizontal **or vertical** red
+triples fits all three. The next emitted query contains a vertical triple and
+separates the rules. All four inputs pass `self_check`; both programs' eight
+outputs were actually executed through protected Racket.
+
+Evidence: `counterexamples/orientation-teaching-lesson.json`; executable probe:
+`workspace/review_tools/teaching_probe.py`. Reproduce from the packet root with
+`python3 review.py run python3 generators/427d6a7812dd/workspace/review_tools/teaching_probe.py --out ../checks/427d6a7812dd/new-witness.json`.
+
+This is one real generated lesson with a missing teaching contrast, not a
+wrong canonical label or a prevalence estimate. The scan stopped after seeds
+0–14, within its explicit 32-seed cap. Production code is unchanged. Next useful
+repair: ensure visible demonstrations contain both a changed horizontal triple
+and an unchanged vertical triple before queries need the distinction, retaining
+the existing length distractors. Both executable rules and private predictions
+are retained for optional alternative-solution research without adding a second
+official answer.
